<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<network-security-config>
    <!-- Cleartext hosts have to be named one by one. Android blocks plain HTTP
         everywhere else, and what it produces ("CLEARTEXT communication to X
         not permitted by network security policy") surfaces as a version row
         reading 查不到: an error message about a policy rather than about
         anything the user did.

         No host is listed today. The version service moved to
         https://api.heyandee.com and CodeFlying to https://baas.kuafuai.net,
         so both cleartext holes were deleted rather than left behind: an
         exception for a host nobody calls only widens what the app will talk
         to in the clear. A build pointed at a plain-HTTP backend has to name
         that host here (and in the debug copy). -->
</network-security-config>
